(g2) d c d f g f e d , a g e g f e d || a C D a g a a , a g a g f e d , f g d e d c , e f e d | a C D a g a a , a g a g f e d , f g d e d c e f e d || A c d f g e'd , c f e d e c d | f a g a f g f'e d , d g f g a g f g f'e d || A c d f g e'd , c f e d e c d | f a g a f g f'e d , d g f g a g f g f'e d || a C D a a g a a , a C g f e d , c f e g a a , f g f'e d || de'd cd' , c f e'd d |||
w: Ví-cti-mae pa-schá-li lau-des ím-mo-lent Chri-sti-á-ni. A-gnus red-é-mit o-ves: Chri-stus ín-no-cens Pa-tri re-con-ci-li-á-vit pec-ca-tó-res. Mors et vi-ta du-él-lo con-fli-xé-re mi-rán-do: dux vi-tae mór-tu-us re-gnat vi-vus. Dic no-bis Ma-rí-a: Quid vi-dí-sti in vi-a? Se-púl-crum Chri-sti vi-vén-tis et gló-ri-am vi-di re-súr-gen-tis; An-gé-li-cos te-stes su-dá-ri-um et ve-stes. Sur-ré-xit Chris-tus spes me-a, prae-cé-det su-os in Ga-li-lae-am. Sci-mus Chri-stum sur-re-xís-se a mór-tu-is ve-re. Tu, no-bis, vi-ctor Rex, mi-se-ré-re! A-men, al-le-lú-ia.
